CODEGEN.md §3.5, §7.9, DECISIONS 403: the Badge shape. The cases of a variant give its kind enum members, which a define of a package the variant's package does not read (an enum with @cpp(defines:)) equals: E8005 foreignDefine at the case.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Requirements; the defines keep the legacy names.
enum Requirement @codes(UInt8) @cpp(defines: "BADGE_REQ_") {
  /// Uses an item.
  USE_ITEM = 5
  /// Reaches a faery rank.
  FAERY_RANK = 6
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: types }
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A badge.
variant Badge {
  /// The item case, named like a's define.
  BADGE_REQ_USE_ITEM {
    /// The item.
    item: Int
  }
  /// The plain case.
  plain
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/b", namespace: "b", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  b/b.canon:6:3
  BADGE_REQ_USE_ITEM is declared for b.Badge.BADGE_REQ_USE_ITEM and written as a #define for a.Requirement.USE_ITEM, in a package this one does not read, so its headers cannot guard it; rename b.Badge.BADGE_REQ_USE_ITEM with @cpp(name:), or use a type of that package here

